{"title":"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(more_formal_explanations_for_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (more formal explanations for Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(No_Coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (No Coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A car travels due east at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcfeb8cb09b8af3dae2cf162c738f90021a90849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> mile per minute on a long, straight road. At the same time, a circular storm, whose radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> miles, moves southeast at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f8db38bc628bf8b47e2de85f08080c519d50cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"37\" /> mile per minute. At time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a607fd61885c014512c949fee18869690330407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=0$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, the center of the storm is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79dc7d13216568e73c831d7b8c14c1a30f7831a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> miles due north of the car. At time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec6f2a97b0f86f2cbec59ec15c5e7680e15f583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> minutes, the car enters the storm circle, and at time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d5b2c7fbdf8c6e2abe1b058e852da3fa50b5f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=t_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, the car leaves the storm circle. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8aabaf15a3974d2e504c41daa2fa52ec1d3451f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12(t_1+t_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We set up a coordinate system, with the starting point of the car at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Origin\" title=\"Origin\">origin</a>. At time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, the car is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789ab25af3a69d03fa430bbed8f9c157cd0dd884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac 23t,0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"59\" height=\"43\" /> and the center of the storm is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c51add26eb39aa7cca8f8be65f7df9ccf1e1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{t}{2}, 110 - \\frac{t}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"106\" height=\"43\" />. Using the distance formula, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c8a2d85f116efaaf7eecb964817e46ee31b231.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}t - \\frac 12t\\right)^2 + \\left(110-\\frac{t}{2}\\right)^2} &amp;\\le&amp; 51\\\\ \\frac{t^2}{36} + \\frac{t^2}{4} - 110t + 110^2 &amp;\\le&amp; 51^2\\\\ \\frac{5}{18}t^2 - 110t + 110^2 - 51^2 &amp;\\le&amp; 0\\\\ \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"301\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p>Noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bccd913671498b646a677b43861eb7d4de47f321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 \\left(t_1+t_2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> is at the maximum point of the parabola, we can use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a67231c240173c653b851b16e1016c2c2fe48e86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{b}{2a} = \\frac{110}{2 \\cdot \\frac{5}{18}} = \\boxed{198}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"169\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28more_formal_explanations_for_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(more_formal_explanations_for_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (more formal explanations for Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (more formal explanations for Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First do the same process for assigning coordinates to the car. The car moves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> miles per minute to the right, so the position starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/670fd20ff3b59885e1f91eb4e08dfb3eb73740ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2}{3}t, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"65\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>Take the storm as circle. Given southeast movement, split the vector into component, getting position <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/779f5190576d6a1f7b15185e2ebc4178e05df93a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{2}t, 110 - \\frac{1}{2}t\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"125\" height=\"45\" /> for the storm's center. This circle with radius 51 yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd2000f1b094e37743d8526029351a93df644c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x - \\frac{1}{2}t\\right)^2 + \\left(y -110 + \\frac{1}{2}t\\right)^2 = 51^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"294\" height=\"48\" />. \n</p><p>Now substitute the car's coordinates into the circle's:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70e2f465b4fb8368e7ce0508f71161dcd5e42e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2}{3}t - \\frac{1}{2}t\\right)^2 + \\left(-110 + \\frac{1}{2}t\\right)^2 = 51^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"286\" height=\"48\" />. \n</p><p>Simplifying and then squaring:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd5f92674eb961329113f77b0798f9d2fb3f18c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{6}t\\right)^2 + \\left(-110 + \\frac{1}{2}t\\right)^2 = 51^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"244\" height=\"48\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27fcb3f18a01d5425042c8354a19d6477e355fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{36}t^2 + \\frac{1}{4}t^2 - 110t + 110^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"197\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\nForming into a quadratic we get the following, then set equal to 0, since the first time the car hits the circumference of the storm is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab09eb0e14820db6dabcda6e9cc8638044351ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and the second is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2ba5789eea835bf50c7be61de92a6c2914e5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fce6feed8273f29b5c416d821e7b1709e69d145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{18}t^2 - 110t + 110^2 - 51^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"230\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe problem asks for sum of solutions divided by 2 so sum is equal to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed22117cbbb6acaaab96a6150061f643cf90bea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{-110}{\\frac{5}{18}} = 110\\cdot{\\frac{18}{5}} = 396\\cdot{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\boxed{198}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"339\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28No_Coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(No_Coordinates)\">Solution 3 (No Coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (No Coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We only need to know how the storm and car move relative to each other, so we can find this by subtracting the storm's movement vector from the car's.  This gives the car's movement vector as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c15ccc61f9f11836c80972dabba5c532f6be87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{6}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"45\" />.  Labeling the car's starting position A, the storm center B, and the right triangle formed by AB with a right angle at B and the car's path, we get the following diagram, with AD as our desired length since D is the average of the points where the car enters and exits the storm.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48fe3e02d7487681f231b87d4a900b423738b15a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200,200); draw((0,0)--(0,110)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,0),S); dot((0,0)); dot((0,110)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,110),NE); draw(circle((0,110),51)); draw((0,0)--(161/3,161.0),EndArrow); draw((0,110)--(110/3,110.0)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(110/3,110.0),SE); dot((110/3,110.0)); label(&quot;D&quot;,(33,99),SE); dot((33,99)); draw((0,110)--(33,99)); markscalefactor=1; draw(rightanglemark((0,110),(33,99),(0,0))); [/asy]\" width=\"205\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62de8cb092ec2c48ea6483a802b863aff8ca6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d315c9216acb8ea07f1dc0a91996cc20de9d184f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB = \\frac{110}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />.  The Pythagorean Theorem then gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db70db275bfee4633cdf27e6407424490115ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\frac{110\\sqrt{10}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"43\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d0c8f318a131898e1e3a872bdf1f68a598aae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABC \\sim \\bigtriangleup ADB$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecdde2869b0076976c48846f87f21abda85ce9d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = (AB)\\frac{AB}{AC} = 33\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"206\" height=\"39\" />.  The Pythagorean Theorem now gives the car's speed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c162b2c8ef49829d0b93147bc3252495d02d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{18}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"42\" height=\"45\" />, and finally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04503a648b1dec6ffb9158c6495983b2fd6ff9e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{33\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{18}}} = \\boxed{198}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"120\" height=\"61\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME\" title=\"1997 AIME\">1997 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016222542\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 255/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7546/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.401      1 -total\n 56.23%    7.535      1 Template:AIME_box\n 42.12%    5.645      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key w